# Line endings. UrbanLens is deployed on Linux and everything that consumes
# these files at runtime is a Linux process - shell scripts under bin/ and
# docker-entrypoint.sh are the sharp edge, since a CRLF shebang line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r" and the container dies with a
# bare "no such file or directory". So the repository stores LF, and a Windows
# checkout adapts rather than the other way round.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes on the way *in* (git converts to LF when it writes the
# index), and `eol=lf` checks out LF on every platform, so a Windows editor that
# saves CRLF still commits LF and a `core.autocrlf=true` setting cannot
# reintroduce it. This is the durable half of the fix: unlike a pre-commit hook,
# it does not depend on anyone having installed one.
#
# Auto-detection still applies - git will not touch a file it detects as binary
# - but the formats below are declared explicitly so nothing hinges on that
# detection, and so `git diff` does not try to render them.
#
# History note: docker-compose.yml and .env-sample were silently converted to
# CRLF in 1379afd9b, which made both conflict as whole files against every
# in-flight branch. That is the failure this file prevents.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary

# Fonts
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

# Archives and documents
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary

# ESRI shapefile components (sample_data/sample_shapefile). Only .prj and .cpg
# are text; the rest are binary and a normalization pass would corrupt them.
*.shp binary
*.shx binary
*.dbf binary

# Geometry fixtures are hex-encoded ASCII rather than real binary, so they
# normalize safely - but they are read with read_bytes() by
# test_import_wkt_wkb.py, so they are called out here as files whose exact
# bytes a test does look at.
*.wkb text eol=lf
*.wkt text eol=lf
